      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Annu Aggarwal has been charged with Section 14 of Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act, 1986."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fd23be16d2e44f72917ba1335cb45820_62",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Same has been reproduced under for reference:\nSection 14. Penalties.-\n(1) Whoever employs any child or permits any child to work in contravention of the provisions of section 3 shall be punishable with imprisonment for a term which shall no"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9932fcf094f74485af24611534845970_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(2) \"Whoever, having been convicted of an offence under section 3, commits a like offence afterwards, he shall be punishable with imprisonment for a term which shall not be less than six months but which may extend to two years."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "63363e83880149519b5e69b7edc795ad_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(3) Whoever-(a) fails to give notice as required by section 9; or (b) fails to maintain a register as required by section 11 or makes any false entry in any such register; or (c) fails to display a notice containing an abstract of section 3"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b94062156ae04200b6eef040f183f57a_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "15. It is also pertinent to make reference to Section 3 of Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation)\nAct, 1986 and Section 2 (ii) which defines child."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6795941d72e94c2892b706522954db15_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Both have been reproduced under for reference:\n2. (ii) \"child\" means a person who has not completed his fourteenth year of age;\nNIDHI Digitally signed by NIDHI SINGH SINGH Date: 2024.02.28 17:30:48 +0530 3."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8ac8a7c1c8a544279ff25b3288dd820b_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Prohibition of employment of children in certain occupations and processes- No child shall be employed or permitted to work in any of the occupations set forth in Part A of the Schedule or in any State vs Annu Aggarwal on 28 February, 2024 "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "aa9aa8daab8a49a3a83903885e546890_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The case of the prosecution, as sought to be established, falls within Part A of Schedule of Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act, 1986 at Point 14."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "da596d37942145ff82cad250a949c083_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Same has been reproduced under for reference:\n\"....(14) Employment of children as domestic workers or servants;...\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4ecb9ffadca4447ab7ed7f7a7b1837f0_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n17. Coming to the testimonies of prosecution witnesses, PW-1/Ms. Pooja herself has stated in her evidence recorded on 28.06.2017 that she is 17/18 years of age."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1349d4be05a649a4bfcd3a54ea0a0334_71",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The alleged employment at the house of the accused is stated to have been done in April 2016 which makes her 16 years of age at the time of her employment."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6378ea5519c04a57ad70053bef7a7422_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The husband of Ms. Pooja ie Mr. Arjun/DW-1 has been examined in Court who has admitted that she was 15 years of age in the year 2016 and that he got married to her in the year 2019."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e268ac27089649ddbca1f818389bcc97_73",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further, mother of Ms. Pooja ie PW-2/ Ms. Guddi has also stated in her evidence recorded on 21.03.2018 that \"...Today my daughter is 18 years of age...\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "40872ac93f80401f9a99c43d2f5de293_74",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "She has further stated in her evidence that she used to take her daughter along with her to play with the children."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ffbea354e4204b89bdd4707f484ed902_75",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "She has further stated in her cross examination that at the time of death of her husband in 2009, her daughter was 8-10 years of age and that her son Deepak was 10-12 years of age."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6fffa44d57e9496ba07b7ddb6e819d24_76",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Her husband was illiterate but only knew how to append his signatures."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d85bb541a3a64dfaaa3419bbc886916d_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "She has further stated that she had gotten her daughter Ms. Pooja admitted in school and at the time of admission in school, Pooja's age was 7 NIDHI Digitally signed by NIDHI SINGH SINGH Date: 2024.02.28 17:30:54 +0530 years and that affida"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e7f0665db0404544863568a781e274a1_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "PW-4 has stated in his cross examination that Mr. Deepak, brother of Ms. Pooja, was 20 years old on 27.06.2016 and had lodged a missing complaint."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9685186ddfe548a2b6d9aef35e79875f_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Prosecution has tried to establish the age of Ms. Pooja only through the school documents received from the concerned School."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0243a3cd64234ff0bb82c614b10841fc_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No bone ossification test report is on record and there is no birth certificate also on record to prove the exact age of Ms. Pooja."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9f921b66c12d487e8702b5177cdeaa34_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Further, PW-3/ Ms.\nReeta Singh, primary school teacher from SDMC Primary Girls School, Devli Village has reflected in her evidence that no birth documents such as birth certificate issued by MCD were seen at the time of admission in School."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "59d441f2a7004400818c50662b63dd9a_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 10 of the Child Labour Act states that if any question arises between an Inspector and an occupier as to the age of any child who is employed or is permitted to work by him in an establishment, the question shall, in the absence of "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "17cdd3a6288542ada77ef111e688601d_83",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case, IO has not taken due steps to confirm the age of the victim from a medical authority."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c12336c41cec457ab04000f930b3850d_84",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "18. In criminal jurisprudence, an accused is presumed to be innocent, until proven guilty, and the burden of proving the guilt of the accused solely rests upon the prosecution by leading positive evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0317b4b472824734ab9b7eac5bcf4069_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Accused is not expected to prove his innocence to the hilt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a3d00792c99047d2b5519cf97a186979_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If the prosecution appears to be State vs Annu Aggarwal on 28 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/76286395/\n5 improbable or lacks credibility the benefit of doubt necessarily has to go to the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "624adcb94ff14164b6012938e67b2825_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The guilt of the accused is not to be proved by mere preponderance of probabilities but it has to be proved beyond all reasonable doubts."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f8c9f41a8ddf4021a79f1e2560cc33c6_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is for the prosecution to travel the entire distance from \"may have\"\nto \"must have\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0cc22f7b17184348aba5d49aa2799997_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Suspicion, howsoever grave, cannot take the place of proof."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4950370a90ed4cb89370dba77cf7f72f_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, in view of the foregoing analysis, this court is of the considered view that the aforesaid deficiencies in the case of the prosecution are sufficient to raise a doubt on the veracity of the entire prosecution case against the accused "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8b7048cbfdc3459b8398be1e2233bf6e_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Prosecution has miserably failed in proving its case beyond reasonable doubt that Ms. Pooja was firstly under 14 years of age in April 2016 and that she was employed by the accused as a domestic worker."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0467b55038bf418c992812556203d1c8_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAccordingly, accused Annu Aggarwal stands acquitted of the offence under Section 14 of Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act, 1986 in the present case."
    },
